<http://data.silknow.org/object/cdbde810-2010-3f79-9443-e0861b1bbcec/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Coral-coloured ribbon (faded from a bright salmon red, still evident on the back of the fabric) with a geometric textured weave in the ground, and a sprig pattern created by metal brocading wefts in a comber repeat. The sprig is composed of berries and foliage in two different qualities of gilded silver thread (flat - <i>lame</i>, and wound round a beige-coloured silk core - <i>filé</i>). the edge is wavy, not quite scalloped. The pattern displays a very economical use of metal, there being very little floating across the reverse side. XRF analysis confirms the metal thread is predominantly silver, with small amounts of copper and gold."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdbde810-2010-3f79-9443-e0861b1bbcec> .

